/-!
# Degree-one primes and the pole of the Dedekind zeta function

For a number field `K`, the sum `∑ 𝔭, N(𝔭) ^ (-s)` over the nonzero prime ideals `𝔭` of `𝓞 K`
is `-log (s - 1) + O(1)` as `s → 1⁺` (`FrobeniusDensity.primeSum_toReal_add_log_isBigO`). The
proof compares this sum with `log ζ_K(s)`, where `ζ_K` is the Dedekind zeta function. The two are
not equal: by the Euler product, `log ζ_K(s)` also contains the terms of the prime powers `𝔭 ^ k`
with `k ≥ 2`. These terms are bounded: for real `s > 1`,
`∑ 𝔭, N(𝔭) ^ (-s) ≤ log ζ_K(s) ≤ ∑ 𝔭, N(𝔭) ^ (-s) + 2 ζ_K(2)`. So the prime sum and `log ζ_K(s)`
differ by `O(1)` as `s → 1⁺`, and they have the same leading term: since `ζ_K` has a simple pole at
`s = 1`, `log ζ_K(s) = -log (s - 1) + O(1)`.

The primes of residue degree at least two contribute `O(1)`, and so does any finite set of primes.
Hence, for every finite set `S₀` of natural numbers, the sum over the primes of `𝓞 K` of residue
degree one lying over primes outside `S₀` is also `-log (s - 1) + O(1)`
(`FrobeniusDensity.degOneSum_add_log_isBigO`). `FrobeniusDensity.DegOneAsymptotic` packages this
for the fixed fields of a Galois extension `L/ℚ`, as in the source.

## Main results

* `FrobeniusDensity.primeSum_toReal_add_log_isBigO`: the prime ideal sum is
  `-log (s - 1) + O(1)` as `s → 1⁺`.
* `FrobeniusDensity.summable_degOne_term` and `FrobeniusDensity.degOneSum_add_log_isBigO`: the
  degree-one prime series converges for `s > 1` and is `-log (s - 1) + O(1)` as `s → 1⁺`.
* `FrobeniusDensity.degOneAsymptotic`: the source's statement `FrobeniusDensity.DegOneAsymptotic`
  for the fixed fields of a Galois extension of `ℚ`.
-/

noncomputable section



namespace FrobeniusDensity

open NumberField Ideal

variable (L : Type*) [Field L] [NumberField L] [IsGalois ℚ L]

/-- **Rational prime ideal.** `ratPrimeIdeal ℓ` is the ideal of `ℤ` generated by the natural
number `ℓ`. -/
public abbrev ratPrimeIdeal (ℓ : ℕ) : Ideal ℤ := Ideal.span {(ℓ : ℤ)}

theorem ratPrimeIdeal_ne_bot {ℓ : ℕ} (hℓ : ℓ.Prime) : ratPrimeIdeal ℓ ≠ ⊥ := by
  rw [Ne, Ideal.span_singleton_eq_bot]
  exact_mod_cast hℓ.ne_zero

variable {L}

omit [IsGalois ℚ L] in
theorem ne_bot_of_liesOver_ratPrimeIdeal {ℓ : ℕ} (hℓ : ℓ.Prime) {Q : Ideal (𝓞 L)}
    [Q.IsPrime] [Q.LiesOver (ratPrimeIdeal ℓ)] : Q ≠ ⊥ :=
  Ideal.ne_bot_of_liesOver_of_ne_bot (ratPrimeIdeal_ne_bot hℓ) Q

end FrobeniusDensity

